# Every env file is untracked except the checked-in dev defaults, so a live
# credential cannot be committed by accident.
#
# `.env.local` is where a developer puts their own machine's
# VITE_COMPASS_CALLER_ID (and a bearer, if they ever point the UI at a real
# authenticated door); Vite loads it last, so it overrides `.env.development`.
# A bare `.env` and `.env.production` are ignored for a sharper reason: Vite
# loads `.env` in EVERY mode, production included, and bakes its VITE_* values
# into the built bundle — so a token left there ships.
#
# `.env.development` is the one exception: loopback defaults, no secret, and it
# documents the required keys by existing.
.env*
!.env.development
